.LP
According to Plato, Anaxagoras was one of the first to propose that whatever there is,
is because that this is the best way.
In
.I Phaedo
Plato lets Socrates tell a story
.QP
.ps 10
.vs 12
One day I heard someone reading,
as he said,
from a book of Anaxagoras,
and saying that it is the Mind that directs and is the cause of everything.
I was delighted with this cause and it seemed to me good,
in a way,
that Mind should be the cause of all.
I thought that if this were so,
the directing Mind would direct everything and arrange each thin in the way that was best.
